            <ArticleTitle>Visualization of a cluster of embolic particles causing angiographic no-reflow during percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E210-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiographic no-reflow occurs occasionally during percutaneous coronary intervention in patients with acute myocardial infarction. Recently, we reported that coronary embolic particles can be detected as high-intensity transient signals with the Doppler guidewire. In the present study, the Doppler guidewire revealed that embolization of a cluster of embolic particles liberated by balloon inflation was responsible for angiographic no-reflow.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
